<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philipp von Hutten</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1546</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philipp von Hutten was a German knight who served the Welser bank in its Venezuelan colony, Klein-Venedig. He took part in expeditions into the interior in search of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-dorado">El Dorado</a> and became captain-general in 1540. In 1546, on his return from a long march, he was seized and executed by the Spanish official <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-de-carvajal">Juan de Carvajal</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philipp-von-hutten.jpg" alt="Philipp von Hutten" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Philipp-von-Hutten.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
